      "text_snapshot": "Proposal\nReplace the facts-path semantic machinery — the bundled 31 MB Model2Vec embedder (assets/embedmodel.bin), per-branch vector caches, RRF fusion, and the sqlite-vec cgo variant — with a ~200-line in-process BM25 ranker plus taxonomy/kind/date filters, slotted in at the existing rankFactsFused(rr=nil) seam. Semantic becomes opt-in or is deleted.\nNet: ≈ −3,000 lines (+~1,260 test lines), −31 MB per binary (~47% raw, ~59% of the compressed download), −1 build variant, −~300 MB peak RSS per query.\nEvidence\n1,748 live Claude Code agent runs (~$365) across two repos (entire-brain, marvin), three models, corpus sizes 5→1,209 facts. Each task is a real captured session's opening request; gold labels are that session's distilled facts, judge-refined and fixed before any arm ran. One agent per (task, arm, model), identical prompt and budget — only the search tool differed. Paired Wilcoxon per cell; deterministic grading (fact IDs in the final answer vs gold).\nArms: brain query (shipped hybrid = lexical + embeddings + RRF) · naive term-match CLI · grep (Read/Grep/Glob over facts files export) · rank2 = BM25 + --path/--kind/--since filters + --list-paths (the proposed replacement, tested as a Python prototype; the Go port is the same deterministic algorithm).\nAgent recall and token cost, semantic → rank2\n| Model | Facts | Tasks | Recall | Tokens/task | Verdict | |---|---|---|---|---|---| | sonnet | up to 878 | 149 | 0.629 → 0.692 | 218k → 157k (−28%) | rank2 better (p=0.022; precision too, p=0.006) | | haiku 4.5 | up to 878 | 149 | 0.618 → 0.563 | 307k → 251k (−18%) | semantic marginal (p=0.051, precision tied) | | fable 5 | up to 878 | 60 | 0.513 → 0.595 | 194k → 180k | rank2 ahead (p=0.07) | | sonnet | 1,209 | 79 | 0.317 → 0.326 | 256k → 203k (−20%) | tie (p=0.88) |\nNaive grep is NOT the proposal — it collapses on weak models (0.215) and at scale (0.154). The ranked top-k interface is load-bearing; BM25 + filters supplies it without the model.\nResources (measured, 1,209-fact corpus)\n| | semantic hybrid | rank2 prototype | |---|---|---| | peak RSS/query | 316 MB (embedder ≈ 111 MB of it) | 14 MB | | latency/query | 0.60 s | 0.12 s | | disk | 19 MB store + 2.4 MB vectors + 31 MB model/binary | 4.8 MB flat files (Go port reads the store in-process) |\nWhy semantic loses its rationale\nStatic ranking: semantic beats Brain's own lexical arm (+0.36 useful/1k, p\u003c0.0001, consistent with the 2026-06-09 ledger row) — but naive grep ALSO beats Brain's lexical arm (p=0.0003), and BM25 beats semantic single-shot at scale (recall@10 0.202 vs 0.170).\nAgentic: the paraphrase-recall edge vanishes once the agent can reformulate (low-overlap stratum tie, p=0.88). Semantic's former large-corpus edge was query-set diversity, which --list-paths → --path narrowing replicates.\nBugs found (fix regardless of this decision)\nProposal-queue poisoning: with 91,364 pending reconcile proposals (mass facts promote --keep-both; 13.5 MB of proposals vs 6.8 MB of facts), brain query silently returns query-blind results in ALL modes — flat positional scores, gold facts absent for their own exact text, no error.\nLossy promote: facts promote --strategy prefer-target promoted 114 of 876 facts into an EMPTY branch.\nScope and caveats\nKnown gap: marginal recall edge for semantic on haiku-class models (p=0.051, precision tied, rank2 still cheaper). The Embedder seam is cheap to keep as an opt-in escape hatch for small-model fleets.\nShared plumbing decision: the dark Gemma/ollama history+conversation fusion arms use the Embedder interface — keep interface + ollama backend, or delete those arms (~1,000 more lines) in the same change.\nContract migrations: --semantic flags → no-op warnings; capabilities --json reports semantic: false (don't drop fields — committed agent-guides parse them); retrieval_engine identity changes; fusion regression tests retired; eval-ledger rows superseding the 2026-06-09 fusion default-on decision; session_privacy_verify stops expecting vector-store artifacts.\nNot tested: corpora ≫1,200 facts, non-Claude models, multi-rep variance (1 rep/task/arm, n=149 paired per cell). Labels are judge-refined silver. The project-file semantic index (refresh index/seed) is a separate pipeline and a separate decision — nothing in this work justifies it either.\nPlan\nGo port of BM25 + filters as the default facts arm (behind rankFactsFused's existing nil-reranker seam).\nRemove the static embedder + assets/embedmodel.bin from the default build; delete vector stores (documented regenerable, never load-bearing).\nDecide the dark fusion arms (keep ollama opt-in vs delete).\nContract migrations + docs/benchmarks.md + ledger rows.\nProposal-queue bug filed and fixed independently.\nReproducibility\nTask sets, all 1,748 run records, grading/analysis scripts, and the prototype CLIs live in .context/semantic-eval/ on branch brain-semantic-search-eval (workspace-local). Durable facts: fact:788fcf552ff68bc5eb85aff6 (matrix determination), fact:55e75df200666f346ff35ea3 (rank2 result), fact:fe39329846002f8ba58387e1 (proposal-queue bug). Any cell re-runs with one command via phase_b.py.\n🤖 Generated with Claude Code",
